# Format, one exchange a line, in the order the run logged them:
#   H <idx> <group>/<id> <run>:<line> <hex>
#       a command the host wrote: its 8-byte header, then its payload. Every byte
#       is the run's: derived from the run's build and its logged inputs, two
#       ways, and the two agree (spec/evidence/traces-derivation.log).
#   D <what> <run>:<line> <hex> rec=<hex>
#       a packet the device wrote into a receive buffer: its 4-byte length-and-
#       flags word, its 4-byte header (identifier, group, sequence), then its
#       payload. rec= is a mask, bit for bit: a set bit was recorded by the run;
#       a clear bit was not, and holds the value the specification's rule gives
#       where it gives one (an answer's identifier, a notification's group 0 and
#       sequence bit 15), else 0.
#   D <what> <run>:<line> unrecorded <count>
#       packets the run counted and did not record.
#   E <what> <run>:<line> <dwords>
#       a device-memory table the host read, dword by dword, as logged.
# The station's address is replaced, everywhere, by 02:00:00:00:00:01.
# Run13: spec/runs/demo-v13.log, the AX200 on the AMD bench, from the alive notification through a passive scan.
